# Security Logging & Monitoring Reviewer Rule v1.0 STRICT

**Do not inline-audit.** Invoke **`security_logging_monitoring_reviewer`** -> `.cursor/agents/security_logging_monitoring_reviewer.md`.

## References

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Policy | `.cursor/skills/security_logging_monitoring_reviewer/POLICY.md` |
| Scan skill | `.cursor/skills/security_logging_monitoring_reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| Report path | `AI/agents/security_reviewers/security_logging_monitoring_reviewer/security_logging_monitoring_reviewer_report.md` |
| Report line | `security_logging_monitoring_reviewer v1.0 STRICT` |
| Fleet position line | `#25 — Phase 8 (Platform & assurance)` |

**POLICY.md wins.**

## Invoke when

Use before deploy or when logging frameworks (`logback`, `log4j`), `MDC` context filters, global exception handlers, authentication listeners, or sensitive `toString()` methods change.

Skip for generated output, `target/`, `node_modules/`, and docs-only edits unless the docs define logging policies.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Logging raw passwords, tokens, API keys, or session IDs is always FAIL.**
2. **Failing to log authentication and authorization failures is always FAIL.**
3. **Omitting correlation context (MDC) for security events is always FAIL.**

## Finding table

Every finding includes:

| Row | Content |
|---|---|
| Evidence | Bad line or runtime proof from project |
| Picture in your head | Mandatory `#### Picture in your head` mental model / analogy / before-after; prefer **In even simpler terms...** or **Here's a practical example:** |
| Policy Rule | POLICY.md - CHECK-ID - citation |
| Pattern | SKILL.md section 8 pattern |
| Mechanism | Plain English + framework/API names |
| Security property | What must be true after fix |
| Prohibited | Short label only |
| Verify | Action + pass signal |

Allowed verdicts: **PASS**, **FAIL**, **MANUAL_REVIEW**, **N/A**. `UNCLEAR` is forbidden.
